Subject: Adds a register-VM profile build that records per-site, per-call and per-function hotness

What this does
  Adds a register-VM profile build that records per-site, per-call and per-function hotness.

Why we need it
  AOT compilation needs to know which functions and which opcodes actually run, and the register VM routes every opcode through one loop only in its non-threaded monolith form, so counting can see them all there and nowhere else.

What it adds
  `JSAotProfSite`/`JSAotProfCall`/`JSAotProfFunc`, hooks in `REGVM_NEXT`, the `js_regvm_execute` entry, both `SET_REG_P` definitions, the register PIC fills and the five monolith call handlers; an `aot_prof` field on `JSFunctionBytecode`; `QJS_AOT_PROFILE` rejected by `#error` outside `QJS_REGVM=1 QJS_REGVM_THREAD=0 QJS_REGVM_ASM=0 QJS_REGVM_RECORD=0`; C callees named by `dladdr` with a `/proc/self/exe` `.symtab` fallback (`-no-pie`).

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
